  "name": "Question 17",
  "problem": "If $A={-2,2}$ and $B={c,d},$ which of the following elements belong to $(A\\times B)\\times B?$\n\n- $(-2,d,c)$\n- $(-2,(c,d))$\n- $((2,d),c)$",
  "worked_solution": "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\nIn this case, $A\\times B$ consists of every combination of ${-2,2}$ with ${c,d},$ as shown in the schematic below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14123139/assets/98e7cfca515290b952ea5aefc9b2516a5cd6a68de0dc048c2075128e6c60b651.png)\n\nHence, the set $A\\times B$ is given by\n\n$$\nA\\times B={(-2,c),(-2,d),(2,c),(2,d)}.\n$$\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n|A\\times B|=|A|\\cdot |B|=2\\cdot 2=4.\n$$\n\nNow, the Cartesian product\n\n$$\n(A\\times B)\\times B\n$$\n\nconsists of every combination of $A\\times B$ and $B,$ as shown in the schematic below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14123139/assets/1e96aeb1c5bfb1f9faa590a8eb8b01528a1ce9431a3f1ceac92b156a9bdde221.png)\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n|(A\\times B)\\times B|=|A\\times B|\\cdot |B|=4\\cdot 2=8.\n$$\n\nFrom the given options, we see that only $((2,d),c)\\in (A\\times B)\\times B.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"",
